---
import learning from '../data/learning.json';
import Shell from '../layouts/Shell.astro';
import {chapters} from '../data/content.json';
---
<Shell title="Is This Actually in the Quran?"><section class="intro"><span class="eyebrow">A reference before a repost</span> <h1>{learning.heading}</h1> <p>Search every ayah in Uthmani Arabic and Pickthall’s English translation. Start with a phrase or a reference.</p></section><section class="panel"><form id="search-form" class="panel-body"><label class="field">Phrase or Quran reference<input id="query" type="search" placeholder="e.g. with hardship, or 94:5-6" maxlength="300" required autocomplete="off" dir="auto"/></label><div class="filters top-gap"><label class="field">Search text<select id="language"><option value="english">Pickthall · English</option><option value="arabic">Uthmani · Arabic (normalized)</option></select></label> <label class="field">Chapter<select id="chapter"><option value="0">All 114 chapters</option>{chapters.map(c=><option value={c.number}>{c.number}. {c.name_simple}</option>)}</select></label> <button class="button" id="submit">Search Quran</button></div> <div class="actions top-gap"><span class="micro">Try a search:</span> {['with hardship','every soul','94:5-6'].map(q=><><button type="button" class="pill" data-example={q}>{q}</button>{' '}</>)}</div><p class="micro">Punctuation and case are ignored. Arabic diacritics, tatweel, and common alif variants are normalized. No stemming or semantic judgment is used.</p><label class="check-label"><input id="remember" type="checkbox"/> Keep up to 5 recent searches in this browser for 30 days</label><div id="recent" class="actions top-gap"></div></form></section><div class="notice top-gap"><p><strong>An empty wording search does not mean “not in the Quran.”</strong> Other translations and paraphrases may express an idea differently. Read the full context and consult qualified scholarship for interpretation.</p></div><section id="results" class="top-gap" aria-live="polite"><div class="empty"><h2>What would you like to check?</h2><p>The local text loads when you run your first search.</p></div></section><noscript><p class="noscript">Local searching requires JavaScript. You can read the source editions through the Sources page.</p></noscript><script>import '../lib/app';</script></Shell>
